rem matmul.pnx - basic bench `matmul`: the product of two n x n integer matrices, a[i] = i + 1 and b[i] = i + 2 in row-major order.
rem pnx matmul.pnx N (default 200, up to 250): c[0] and the acc of all cells mod 1000000007.
use io .
use env .
use str .
const cells 62500
array a int cells
array b int cells
array c int cells
def main or fail do
  1 env.arg or_else to e "200" end str.to_int or_fail to n
  n n mul to sz
  0 sz range do to i i 1 add i set a  i 2 add i set b end each
  0 n range do to i
    0 n range do to j
      0 to acc
      0 n range do to k acc  i n mul k add a idx  k n mul j add b idx mul add to acc end each
      acc  i n mul j add set c
    end each
  end each
  0 to total
  0 sz range do to i total i c idx add 1000000007 mod to total end each
  args "matmul " n " " 0 c idx " " total . cat io.println
end
main or_else to e args "matmul: " e err_text . cat io.println end
